+For the local KVMem ring with `--max-concurrency 1`, `NINFER_KVMEM_INDEX_HOST=1`
+stores the mean-K index in explicitly mapped pinned Host memory. Unset or `0`
+keeps it in Device memory. The Host route retains the same ordered F32 sums,
+counts and CUDA kernels; scoring uploads each populated layer into one reused
+Device scratch buffer on the scoring stream. For 16 full-attention layers,
+4 KV heads, head dimension 256 and a 262144-token ceiling, the index occupies
+256.25 MiB of Host RAM plus 16 MiB of Device scratch, saving 240.25 MiB of
+Device storage. This allocation is independent of `--host-kv-mib` and is
+reported by the `kvmem_index` warmup log. `NINFER_HOST_PAGEABLE=1` does not
+make this index pageable. The existing ring index is process-local and shared;
+this option does not add concurrent sequence support. Qualify long-context
+recall and end-to-end performance before increasing the Device KV pool.
 
